                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "04f7f256-23fd-3c70-8928-5692c9c4b4d6",
                        "entry_id": "4b56b0aa-da72-3026-996d-08a47950b40e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who advocates for the preservation of natural or man-made landmarks."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d79afbe-1e16-4603-9fee-59d71f68533b",
                                "sense_id": "04f7f256-23fd-3c70-8928-5692c9c4b4d6",
                                "text": "Thanks to cheap storage and easy copying, our digital souls have the potential to be truly immortal. But do we really want everything we’ve done online – offhand comments, camera-phone snaps or embarrassing surfing habits – to be preserved for posterity? One school of thought, the “preservationists”, believes we owe it to our descendants."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f28b4593-720a-44ad-9df1-e4a3b367e785",
                                "sense_id": "04f7f256-23fd-3c70-8928-5692c9c4b4d6",
                                "text": "Last, but very much not least, are the portals of the Ffestiniog Railway's Moelwyn Tunnel. The tunnel's story itself is well told - it was part of the preservationists' deviation required to get around a reservoir that had flooded the earlier route. But the reason for its inclusion here is that it is probably the most recently constructed, properly architected tunnel portal in Britain."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
